**Laboratory showcase.** At the Model workbench, open **Scene document → Definition library → Browse the example parts library**. Import and place both Bracket revisions. Inspect their Steel grades and the shared Millimetre definition. Withhold a requirement, try the dependent import, restore permission and try again. Publish a placement move through **Accepted edits and measurements**, then inspect both Brackets after reopening the destination with the source offline. [Controls, expected results and replay cases](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage05/README.md)

**Handoff** On base `3efe8354` with the recorded changes, `cargo xtask workspace showcase <fresh-output-directory>` passed across five native desktop processes. The first Bracket brought in three definitions. The second brought in two and reused Millimetre. Repeating the import added zero. A fresh desktop resolved both grades with the source offline, preserving three earlier slots, their Room binding and the accepted move. A workspace saved by the Stage 004 binary passed the same import and reopen checks. All 40 warm durable saves met 200 ms, with a 30.469 ms p95 and a 32.186 ms maximum. The binary and the 360 × 700 pointer placement and undo passed. [Captured results and tested source hashes](../../../fixtures/workspace/stage05/verification.json)

